{
  "requirement": "When implementation shows that agreed requirement text must change, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to stop work that depends on the change and take the changed requirements through review, agreement, and commit before continuing.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject `requirements.cli.requirements_review_skill.text_change` has two obligations. When implementation shows agreed text must change, the `habeas-requirements` skill must direct agents to (1) stop work that depends on the change, and (2) take the changed requirements through review, agreement and commit before continuing.\n\nThe only test is `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_stops_dependent_work_when_agreed_text_must_change]`. It covers both obligations.\n\n- **Stop and take through review first.** `assert_phrases` runs `assert_text` over `bundled_skill(\"habeas-requirements\")`. `bundled_skill` collapses whitespace, so the phrase matches even though it wraps across lines in `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`. The assertion requires the exact sentence: \"If implementation shows that agreed text must change, stop work that depends on it and take the changed requirements through steps 3 to 5 first\". That sentence contains the trigger, the stop directive, and the \"first\" ordering that means before continuing. Removing or weakening any of these would fail the test.\n- **Steps 3 to 5 are review, agreement and commit.** The loop uses `step()`, which reads from `workflow_steps`, to assert that step 3 starts with \"Review.\", step 4 with \"Present\" and step 5 with \"Commit.\". Step 4 is the presentation to the user for agreement. This stops the \"steps 3 to 5\" reference from silently pointing at other steps if the workflow is renumbered.\n\nThe requirement concerns the text of a skill document, and the text distinguishes no other modes or input classes. Phrase and step-heading assertions are an adequate check. I found no untested obligation, and no `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "6450b4a7e3b7e32ec2e1acd6785d0e61ab738feb730a829aa78b6ff1e4e8b80f",
